Z||000000||Adrift||11-20-2001||06:59 PM||||I'm thinking:<BR>Front: 17x7, 215/45/WR17 40mm offset<BR>Rear: 17x8,  245/40/WR17 40mm offset <P>Those will fit, correct? Are these "hard to find wheels" - price is an issue here. I know that 355 rebodies make the wheel look like they're really inside the wheel well so you're supposed to use wheel spacers, but I plan on putting the held motor sports wide track suspension in the future (when I get more money). This car is not for racing, its a daily driver.<P>Or should I got for <BR>205/40/18 in front, 245/35/18 in back<BR>like real ferrari's (except they use 18 inch wheels, which I don't believe will fit..?).. I'm thinking that will be WAY to expensive...||||reg||1
